Keep training DataLoader workers alive across epochs.

Without persistent_workers, PyTorch re-forks every worker at the start of each
epoch (~25 s per epoch on Aurora with 8 workers x 12 ranks/node), which
dominates short epochs at scale. Measured on Aurora (full dataset, fp16, JIT):
4 nodes 457 -> 652 samples/s, 16 nodes 758 -> 1230 samples/s.

Applies to sc25-dl-tutorial commit 7e91316 (saforem2 sunspot-xpu-support):
  (setup.sh applies it after checking out that commit)

--- a/utils/data_loader.py
+++ b/utils/data_loader.py
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@
         sampler=sampler,
         worker_init_fn=worker_init,
         drop_last=True,
-        #                            persistent_workers=train,
+        persistent_workers=train and params.num_data_workers > 0,
         pin_memory=torch.cuda.is_available(),
     )
 
